I. Job ProfileJob TitleQuality Control SupervisorDepartmentQuality

Direct SupervisorLead Quality Control SupervisorDirect SubordinatesOutgoing Quality Control

II. Job Summary：
1. Process and product inspection management;
2. Direct and conduct Process and Product audit;
3. Organize summarize and analyze the quality data to monitor the process and improve the quality;
4. Lead, organize and implement analyzing, handling, folloing up, and improving of internal quality issues;
5. Supervise the Outgoing Quality Control inspectors;
6. Conduct risk analysis and decision making.
7. Assist in handling customer complaints
8. Assist second and third party audits

III. Job Functions and Duties

NO.Representative Duties

1Process inspection management:
1.1 Prepare the inspection standard and test specification for product production process and after approval, organize its implementation;
1.2 Establish and maintain production reserved sample(s), defect sample(s) and limit sample(s);
1.3 Supervise relevant personnel to inspect quality of semi-finished and finished product and process quality according to inspection standard and detection specification;
1.4 Prepare MSA plan and organize implementation and propose improvement actions for unacceptable MSA;
1.5 Train operator(s) and online inspector(s) to evaluate and handle with non-conforming products, establish and maintain product repair/rework specifications;
1.6 Collect data and summarize reports for daily, weekly and monthly reviews within the quality department.

2Process and Product audit management:
2.1 Prepare product audit and process audit specification and, after approval, organize its implementation;
2.2 Prepare product audit and process audit plan, implement, track and feed back the implementation and the removal of nonconforming items;
2.3 Participate in product inspections and reviews of samples during new product development, quality gate review before mass production and the process review;
2.4 Participate in the process audit, internal audit and external audit organized by the company;
2.5 Organize regular review of company fixture and mold test tools and recognize and manage process change points.

3Quality problem handling and improvement:
3.1 Timely responses, properly handle quality problems that occurr during production and report material quality abnormality.
3.2 Responsible for handling a customer complaint, return of goods. SOP+3 months and track the effectiveness of corrective and preventive actions working with the customer quality engineer;
3.3 Establish and implement process statistics and analysis, find deficiency in a timely manner or risk point relating to process capability and continuously improve the process and product quality;
3.4 Regularly make statistics and analysis of process quality, timely prepare and report the analysis report.

4Other duties relating to Quality Assurance:
4.1 Responsible for direct supervison of the Quality Control Supervisor within the workshop.
4.2 Responsible for training and verifying operator and online inspector relating to quality inspection skills;
4.3 Responsible for compiling, archiving and transfering materials relating to new product development process.

5Reports to prepare and submit:
Daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly/annual quality reports, process and product audit report

6Other duties as assigned

7Nothing in the Position Description restricts management's right to assign or re-assign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time

